  "body": {
    "drop": [],
    "ops": [
      {
        "fields": {
          "milestone": "36",
          "statement": "An agent conducts each change set and the daemon only ships and guards: one conductor session plans missing leaves, spawns visible builder, verifier and reviewer sessions and lands; a dumb, durable daemon of a few primitives gates, pushes, waits for CI, merges and hands every red back to the conductor; teams bring their own skills, agents and workflows through a gate-checked contract; a change goes from start to merge in 40 minutes or less with planning included, and at most 1 run in 10 needs a person."
        },
        "handle": "milestone-36",
        "id": "01M79KKVJEV4SCGA3BRRQKZC9A",
        "key": "zzzzzzzr",
        "kind": "intent",
        "node": "01M79KKVJEV4SCGA3BRPABPYX8",
        "op": "node.create",
        "parent": null
      },
      {
        "fields": {
          "statement": "One conductor session conducts a change set end to end: it plans the leaves when there are none, spawns a builder and then a verifier per leaf, spawns the Plan, Code and QA review checks with a critic only on a blocker or major finding, spawns a fixer for confirmed findings, and lands the change set on the branch."
        },
        "handle": "m36-conductor",
        "id": "01M79KKVJZBSHJ5RXCG89D8838",
        "key": "i",
        "kind": "intent",
        "node": "01M79KKVJZBSHJ5RXCG4JKBSP4",
        "op": "node.create",
        "parent": "01M79KKVJEV4SCGA3BRPABPYX8"
      },
      {
        "fields": {
          "statement": "The daemon is dumb but durable: workflows are built from the agent, spawn, gate, push/pr, wait, merge, signoff and hook primitives; any red result hands back to a named agent step with the cause, at most three times before the run parks with an inbox item; every step and spawned session is journaled, and killing the daemon at any point loses nothing."
        },
        "handle": "m36-durable-daemon",
        "id": "01M79KKVKEPHJQ6MH0T2M4KVAH",
        "key": "r",
        "kind": "intent",
        "node": "01M79KKVKEPHJQ6MH0SZ58FG2Z",
        "op": "node.create",
        "parent": "01M79KKVJEV4SCGA3BRPABPYX8"
      },
      {
        "fields": {
          "statement": "Every session a run spawns is visible as a child of the run in rhiza run status and the web run page, with its role, leaf, model and outcome, and can be opened or resumed like any other session."
        },
        "handle": "m36-visible",
        "id": "01M79KKVM10T0D703RCSYYYDK7",
        "key": "w",
        "kind": "intent",
        "node": "01M79KKVM10T0D703RCS27QB7M",
        "op": "node.create",
        "parent": "01M79KKVJEV4SCGA3BRPABPYX8"
      },
      {
        "fields": {
          "statement": "A team brings its own skills, agent and workflow: its already-installed skill runs through an invoke template, reads brief.md, slice.json and handback.md, meets the agent contract that the daemon's gates check, and passes rhiza skill check before it runs for real."
        },
        "handle": "m36-byo",
        "id": "01M79KKVMQRDB3EETMZNKJ7XZY",
        "key": "y",
        "kind": "intent",
        "node": "01M79KKVMQRDB3EETMZHRCNATG",
        "op": "node.create",
        "parent": "01M79KKVJEV4SCGA3BRPABPYX8"
      },
      {
        "fields": {
          "statement": "Over the 30 runs on the conductor default after the milestone lands, the median time from a run's start to its merge is 40 minutes or less, including the conductor planning any missing leaves (afk: 37.6 minutes; Rhiza before: about 75)."
        },
        "handle": "m36-40m",
        "id": "01M79KKVNBXPJGA2DYA6XSJZGC",
        "key": "z",
        "kind": "intent",
        "node": "01M79KKVNBXPJGA2DYA47YZZA6",
        "op": "node.create",
        "parent": "01M79KKVJEV4SCGA3BRPABPYX8"
      },
      {
        "fields": {
          "statement": "Over the same 30 runs, at most 3 need a person beyond the owner's own sign-offs and real questions: no hand-driving a ship, killing a process, nudging a session or retrying a step by hand."
        },
        "handle": "m36-touches",
        "id": "01M79KKVNWQJPFDDBJVH72157Q",
        "key": "zi",
        "kind": "intent",
        "node": "01M79KKVNWQJPFDDBJVF43HG00",
        "op": "node.create",
        "parent": "01M79KKVJEV4SCGA3BRPABPYX8"
      },
      {
        "fields": {
          "quote": "we also need to keep in mind that people should be able to bring their own workflows. the daemon should be dumb but durable. the original ask for orchestrating from the daemon was determinism but we're not getting that. the Damon should provide useful hooks for things that agents can't do, or shouldn't do. it should be as flexible as we can make it, but useful.",
          "statement": "Rhiza's runs move from a daemon-driven workflow of about 56 steps to a conductor agent per change set over a dumb, durable daemon of a few primitives, with a gate-checked agent contract so teams bring their own skills, agents and workflows; determinism means durable decisions and deterministic gates, not scripting each agent judgment."
        },
        "handle": "conductor-milestone-direction",
        "id": "01M79KKVPGCBYHVX9H9WC9H6WT",
        "key": null,
        "kind": "decision",
